{
  "title": "Drums Practice",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Read the chart, play the",
        "pad, watch your timing.",
        "",
        "Header: +3 s12 is 3ms",
        "late, a spread of 12.",
        "Narrow is good.",
        "",
        "The bar at the bottom",
        "fills as the drill goes,",
        "hits/misses beside it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "PLAY   listen, unscored",
        "REC    practise, scored",
        "Same button pauses; the",
        "other one switches.",
        "MENU   the drill list",
        "BACK   to the start,",
        "       then up, then out",
        "SHIFT+click  settings",
        "",
        "A result: REC again,",
        "BACK to the start,",
        "CLICK the next drill,",
        "JOG back: look over the",
        "take as you played it.",
        "Only whole takes count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The list",
      "lines": [
        "Basics, the Learning",
        "Path, Grooves,",
        "Rudiments, Training and",
        "Quiz. Progress is last.",
        "",
        "Click opens, Back goes",
        "up. A groove opens its",
        "levels: L0 at your own",
        "pace, then one limb",
        "more each rung.",
        "",
        "A row shows your best",
        "clean speed: 80%. A",
        "tick is learned, a ring",
        "played but not clean."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Own pace (L0)",
      "lines": [
        "L0 is the whole groove,",
        "no clock. The bar stands",
        "still; arrows mark the",
        "next stack.",
        "",
        "Strike its drums, and",
        "only those, TOGETHER",
        "(60ms on normal) and the",
        "arrows move on.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear the bar",
        "REC    begin, or pause",
        "Learned: 90% right 1st",
        "time. The % is your",
        "pace, of the tempo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Knobs",
      "lines": [
        "In a drill:",
        "1  scrub, when stopped",
        "8  speed, 50-120%",
        "",
        "Speed slows any drill,",
        "grooves and rudiments",
        "too. The tempo you play",
        "is what is recorded.",
        "",
        "In settings the knobs",
        "are the rows on screen,",
        "five to a page.",
        "Elsewhere they do",
        "nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The pads",
      "lines": [
        "Left half is your left",
        "hand, right half your",
        "right. Each voice owns a",
        "block; any pad in it",
        "counts.",
        "",
        "kit       the whole kit",
        "sticking  one surface"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Colours",
      "lines": [
        "green   you got it",
        "amber   right drum,",
        "        WRONG HAND",
        "azure   right drum, too",
        "        soft or too loud",
        "red     you missed it",
        "yellow  your finger",
        "violet  now / playing",
        "purple  what is coming",
        "pulse   Study waits here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Study",
      "lines": [
        "Settings > Study stops",
        "the scroll ON a note you",
        "missed. The lane names",
        "it; Guide pads pulse it.",
        "",
        "One press carries on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scoring",
      "lines": [
        "Four things, counted",
        "apart, because each is",
        "fixed differently:",
        "",
        "timing   mean and spread",
        "drum     hit or miss",
        "hand     sticking error",
        "dynamic  accent / ghost"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Accents",
      "lines": [
        "An accent is LOUDER",
        "than your own strokes:",
        "their median + Accent +",
        "(15). A ghost: median",
        "- Ghost - (20).",
        "",
        "Strokes around 68: an",
        "accent needs 83. Hit",
        "everything hard and",
        "nothing stands out.",
        "",
        "Scored apart: dyn 30%.",
        "A soft accent is never",
        "a wrong note. Beside",
        "it: 16 soft 74<83 =",
        "played 74, needed 83."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Clean at tempo",
      "lines": [
        "A drill is learned when",
        "you play it CLEAN at its",
        "written tempo:",
        "",
        "90% of notes right -",
        "right drum and hand,",
        "no strays -",
        "and the spread inside",
        "the Strict window.",
        "",
        "Your % is the fastest",
        "clean take. 100% earns",
        "the tick - but not on",
        "Loose, Guide pads or",
        "Study."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Learning Path",
      "lines": [
        "Four tracks side by",
        "side: Time, Rudiments,",
        "Grooves and Ear.",
        "",
        "Continue opens the next",
        "step of the track you",
        "left longest. Skip next",
        "passes one by. CLICK on",
        "a result goes on.",
        "",
        "Nothing is locked: a",
        "take anywhere counts.",
        "A groove learned at L4",
        "ticks L1-L3 too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Repetition",
      "lines": [
        "What you learned comes",
        "back after 1, 3, 7, 14",
        "and 30 days: a short",
        "daily routine.",
        "",
        "A clean take at tempo",
        "moves it further out; a",
        "slip brings it back",
        "tomorrow. Slow practice",
        "never counts as a slip,",
        "and your best never",
        "drops."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Progress",
      "lines": [
        "Overall and each track:",
        "drills learned, as a",
        "line along real time.",
        "",
        "Then every drill you",
        "played: CLICK for its",
        "takes' chart, the 100%",
        "line dotted, clean",
        "takes filled.",
        "",
        "In a chart the JOG goes",
        "on to the next one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The result",
      "lines": [
        "Big: the speed you",
        "played, % of written.",
        "Beside it: % right and",
        "the spread; the one",
        "that stopped it is",
        "inverted. Not clean:",
        "big is % right, and",
        "under it what cost the",
        "most: 4 wrong hands.",
        "dyn 30%: how accents",
        "and ghosts sounded.",
        "",
        "JOG back: the take as",
        "you played it - rings",
        "hit, crosses missed.",
        "JOG on past the end or",
        "BACK: the result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Ladder",
      "lines": [
        "Starts at 70% of the",
        "drill's tempo and climbs",
        "through it. Play N bars",
        "clean and it goes up.",
        "Slip and the rung plays",
        "again; slip twice and",
        "it stops.",
        "",
        "Your score is the top",
        "clean tempo, kept per",
        "drill and plotted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quiz",
      "lines": [
        "Guess and Hear: drum -",
        "play the drum asked for.",
        "",
        "Pick: drum, Hear:",
        "subdivision and Pick:",
        "groove name what you",
        "heard. Their answers sit",
        "on the bottom row, one",
        "coloured pad each; the",
        "screen names the colour.",
        "Press it, or JOG and",
        "CLICK.",
        "",
        "REC is help; PLAY plays",
        "the question again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Latency",
      "lines": [
        "If every hit reads late",
        "by the same amount, that",
        "is your rig, not you.",
        "",
        "Settings > Latency takes",
        "it off every reading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sound",
      "lines": [
        "The module has its own",
        "kit and click. Nothing",
        "to set up.",
        "",
        "MIDI out can send to a",
        "track or USB instead."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
